  "summary": "Costa Mesa residents and immigrant-rights advocates urged the City Council to terminate its Flock Safety ALPR contract over concerns about data sharing with ICE and federal agencies, an unfulfilled audit request, and a prior officer misuse incident. The council is scheduled to vote July 21 on whether to end the contract, with CMPD expected to deliver an audit and alternatives report.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "An audit on CMPD's use of automated license plate reader camera data, sought in April, has not been produced.",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "citizens discovered Costa Mesa police sought Flock camera data from the two municipalities on behalf of Homeland Security and the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms (ATF), as well as unspecified out-of-state agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "a former Costa Mesa Police Department officer on leave in 2023 illegally accessed camera data to track his wife, an ex-girlfriend and a third person",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "The council is anticipated to vote on whether or not to terminate the city's contract with Flock.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
  ],
